<section id="pipeline" class="border-b border-line">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-20">
    <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-copper">One process</p>
    <h2 class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-3xl font-medium tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">
      Capture, encode, serve. Nothing else in the path.
    </h2>

    <div class="mt-12 grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <article class="rounded-2xl border border-line bg-ink-2 p-6">
        <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-mute">The usual stack</p>
        <ol class="mt-6 space-y-3 font-mono text-sm text-paper-dim">
          <li class="rounded-xl border border-dashed border-line px-4 py-3">Camera API</li>
          <li class="rounded-xl border border-dashed border-line px-4 py-3">FFmpeg / GStreamer</li>
          <li class="rounded-xl border border-dashed border-line px-4 py-3">Separate media server</li>
          <li class="rounded-xl border border-line px-4 py-3 text-paper">Viewer</li>
        </ol>
        <p class="mt-5 text-sm text-mute">Three processes, a multimedia runtime, and a sidecar daemon.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="rounded-2xl border border-copper/40 bg-ink-2 p-6">
        <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-copper">camrtsp</p>
        <ol class="mt-6 space-y-3 font-mono text-sm">
          <li class="rounded-xl border border-line bg-ink-3 px-4 py-3">OS camera · AVFoundation / Media Foundation / Camera2</li>
          <li class="rounded-xl border border-line bg-ink-3 px-4 py-3">OS H.264 · VideoToolbox / MFT / MediaCodec</li>
          <li class="rounded-xl border border-copper/50 bg-ink px-4 py-3 text-copper">In-process RTSP on :8554</li>
          <li class="rounded-xl border border-line px-4 py-3 text-paper-dim">VLC · ffplay · OBS · NVR · Home Assistant</li>
        </ol>
        <p class="mt-5 text-sm text-paper-dim">Late joiners wait at most one GOP. Default is two seconds.</p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-10 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-paper-dim">
      It is a camera publisher, not a media router. It does not transcode foreign streams,
      record to disk, or speak WebRTC. Point
      <a class="text-paper underline decoration-line underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-copper" href="https://github.com/bluenviron/mediamtx">MediaMTX</a>
      or
      <a class="text-paper underline decoration-line underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-copper" href="https://github.com/AlexxIT/go2rtc">go2rtc</a>
      at camrtsp when you want the webcam itself to be the source.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
